<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_CrackedLands.xml               UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-21
  ============================================================================

  FLOODEDCANYON_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 (biome_mod_architecture.md §5 Phase A, §7 Q4 —
  "is RM_FloodedCanyon the Cracked Lands? YES, same place"). Wires the FROZEN
  campaign roster/weather/terrain into `RM_FloodedCanyon`, the def that now
  survives the twin. `RUT_CrackedLands.xml` stays byte-for-byte frozen (one
  header comment only) and carries the live world until the terminal paint;
  this file is what makes `RM_FloodedCanyon` behave identically for anyone
  running the Utinni campaign patches, per §5 step 4.

  🔑 THE SPLIT, and why it is a REPLACE, not an ADD, unlike WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml:
  `the_cracked_lands.md` (FROZEN) §0 and §6 ban 3 are explicit — "the vanilla
  roster (rat, iguana, dromedary, boomalope, boomrat, ostrich, donkey, fennec,
  warg, the insects) is EVICTED" and "No nameable terrestrial animals — the
  vanilla zoo evicts." `RM_FloodedCanyon_Biome.xml`'s own wildAnimals
  (Iguana/Dromedary/Fox_Fennec/Warg/Rat/Cougar) is exactly that evicted
  roster — correct for a non-campaign RimWorld world, banned for this one. So
  the whole dictionary is REPLACED for the campaign, not merged into. Same
  logic for wildPlants (ban 2, "No green outside the shade line," and §4's
  "the vanilla flora... is REPLACED") and for baseWeatherCommonalities (ban 5,
  "No rain in the canyons," which zeroes/repoints values RM_'s own generic
  table already carries non-zero, so an Add would leave the banned weather
  standing alongside the new).

  ROSTER SOURCE: `RUT_CrackedLands.xml`'s own frozen `<wildAnimals>` /
  `<wildPlants>` / `<baseWeatherCommonalities>` — copied verbatim, split into
  two operations only so the RSW_-bestiary-gated entries can carry their own
  MayRequire the way the item's own step 2 asks ("Every RSW_/SW_/RUT_ entry
  ... goes to ... WildAnimals_<Biome>.xml as a PatchOperationAdd ... with
  MayRequire=mandrake.rsw.swbestiary"):
    - Op 1 (unconditional on any donor mod, still PatchOperationConditional-
      guarded on the target node): PatchOperationReplace with the 7 entries
      that are third-party donor content, NOT ours (mlie.starwarsanimal-
      collection's Gornt/Eopie/CanCell/Convor/Woolamander, sarg.alphaanimals'
      AA_Murkling/AA_SandSquid) — each keeps its own inline MayRequire
      exactly as RUT_CrackedLands.xml already carries it (architecture doc
      §7 Q9: "donor fauna inline in RimMandrake defs: ACCEPTABLE, leave them
      inline").
    - Op 2 (MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary"): PatchOperationAdd for the
      3 RSW_-prefixed entries (RSW_MutagenicNorphea, RSW_SandLeaper,
      RSW_Creature_Mantrap) — our own bestiary, so gated on that mod rather
      than left to ride the unconditional block.
  wildPlants (Op 3) and baseWeatherCommonalities (Op 4) are each a single
  unconditional PatchOperationReplace — none of that content is RSW_-gated
  (the 3 RUT_TwistingThorn* plants are this mod's own defs, always loaded
  with UtinniPatches; AB_HardyGrass/AB_GargantuanLithops/GRimMoss carry no
  MayRequire in the source def either, preserved as-is, not this item's scope
  to correct).

  🔑 terrainsByFertility (Op 5): RM_FloodedCanyon_Biome.xml ships a generic
  Sand/Soil split by fertility (soil forms naturally above 0.7 fertility) —
  correct for a generic canyon on any world. `the_cracked_lands.md` §7 rules
  soil is UNIQUELY the flood's product ("actual soil... in the shade... the
  ONLY real soil on the dryland ladder," §1 "leaves behind the one thing
  nowhere else on the dryland ladder has") — natural soil-by-fertility would
  contradict that, so the campaign override replaces the whole table with
  RUT_CrackedLands.xml's own pure-Sand entry (-999~999): all soil here comes
  from FlowWorks' flood mechanic (RM_MapComponent_CanyonFlood), never from
  the terrain generator.

  FISH: RUT_CrackedLands.xml's own inline `<fishTypes>`/`<maxFishPopulation>`
  (FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1 wave 3) is mirrored onto RM_FloodedCanyon as a
  second, parallel operation in `SandFishing_CrackedLands.xml` (this folder's
  sibling, already scoped to this biome's fish) rather than duplicated here —
  one topic, one file.

  DISEASES: the 3 RUT_-only disease entries beyond RM_'s own five
  (Disease_MuscleParasites/FibrousMechanites/SensoryMechanites — plain
  vanilla-Core incidents, Core/Defs/Storyteller/Incidents_Map_Disease.xml, no
  lore attachment) are ported directly into RM_FloodedCanyon_Biome.xml's own
  body instead of patched here — disease-appropriate for any world, not
  campaign flavor (see that file's own comment on the addition).

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validated against the live def dump and the
  active mod set with skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Op 1: the non-RSW_ alien/donor fauna — always loaded with UtinniPatches,
       gated per-entry on their own donor mod exactly as the frozen def does. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildAnimals>
          <Gornt MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.3</Gornt>  <!-- gornt - the-Patient, keep -->
          <Eopie MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.25</Eopie>  <!-- eopie - the-Patient, keep -->
          <CanCell MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.2</CanCell>  <!-- can-cell - flier-commuter, keep -->
          <Convor MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.2</Convor>  <!-- convor - flier-commuter, import -->
          <AA_Murkling MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_Murkling>  <!-- murkling - the-Spenders, adjust-keep -->
          <Woolamander MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.15</Woolamander>  <!-- woolamander - flier-commuter, import -->
          <AA_SandSquid MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_SandSquid>  <!-- sand squid - the-Sealed, adjust-keep -->
        </wildAnimals>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Op 2: OUR OWN RSW_ bestiary entries, gated on that mod per the item's
       own step 2 instruction. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_MutagenicNorphea>0.4</RSW_MutagenicNorphea>  <!-- mutagenic norphea - the-Sealed, keep -->
        <RSW_SandLeaper>0.2</RSW_SandLeaper>  <!-- sand leaper - the-Spenders, adjust-keep -->
        <RSW_Creature_Mantrap>0.15</RSW_Creature_Mantrap>  <!-- mantrap - the-Patient, import -->
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Op 3: the alien flora, replacing RM_'s generic vanilla-core plant list
       wholesale (ban 2: "No green outside the shade line"). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <wildPlants>
          <AB_HardyGrass>1.0</AB_HardyGrass>  <!-- hardy grass -->
          <GRimMoss>0.8</GRimMoss>  <!-- moss -->
          <RUT_TwistingThorngrass>0.5</RUT_TwistingThorngrass>  <!-- twisting thorngrass -->
          <RUT_TwistingThornweed>0.4</RUT_TwistingThornweed>  <!-- twisting thornweed -->
          <RUT_TwistingThornwood>0.2</RUT_TwistingThornwood>  <!-- twisting thornwood - tree -->
          <AB_GargantuanLithops>0.15</AB_GargantuanLithops>  <!-- gargantuan lithops -->
        </wildPlants>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Op 4: the weather ban (ban 5 — no rain in the canyons; no basis for
       snow either). Replaces the whole dictionary rather than adding to it,
       since RM_'s own table already carries non-zero Rain/SnowGentle/
       SnowHard that must read as banned, not merely supplemented. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/baseWeatherCommonalities</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/baseWeatherCommonalities</xpath>
      <value>
        <baseWeatherCommonalities>
          <Clear>85</Clear>
          <DryThunderstorm>3</DryThunderstorm>
          <Sandstorm MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">8</Sandstorm>
          <Fog>0</Fog>
          <Rain>0</Rain>
          <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
          <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
          <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
          <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
        </baseWeatherCommonalities>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Op 5: soil is uniquely the flood's product here (§7) — no natural
       soil-by-fertility band, pure sand until FlowWorks floods a cell. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/terrainsByFertility</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FloodedCanyon"]/terrainsByFertility</xpath>
      <value>
        <terrainsByFertility>
          <li>
            <terrain>Sand</terrain>
            <min>-999</min>
            <max>999</max>
          </li>
        </terrainsByFertility>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
